      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "ผม and ฉัน",
      "text": "ผม is \"I\" for a man; ฉัน is \"I\" for a woman. Thai often leaves \"I\" out when it is clear who is speaking, as in ชื่อแซมครับ. คุณ is the polite \"you\".",
      "explains": [
        "th.pronoun-i"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    }
  ],
